# §4.27 Sums
%%%
number := false
%%%

Source: [DLMF §4.27](https://dlmf.nist.gov/4.27).

Section 4.27 is a reference section rather than a formula section.  It
contains no numbered equations, tables, figures, or additional displayed
identities.  For sums of trigonometric and inverse-trigonometric functions,
the DLMF points readers to the following standard compendia:

- Gradshteyn and Ryzhik (2015), Chapter 1;
- Hansen (1975), §§14–42;
- Oberhettinger (1973); and
- Prudnikov et al. (1986a), Chapter 5.

The neighboring DLMF sections provide the mathematical source context:
[§4.26 Integrals](https://dlmf.nist.gov/4.26) precedes this bibliography, and
[§4.28 Definitions and Periodicity](https://dlmf.nist.gov/4.28) follows it.
Since the source contributes bibliography only, this page records that prose
directly and introduces no mathematical declaration or quantitative companion.
